# Local development environment for `go run ./test`.
#
# Copy this file to test/.env and fill in what you need. test/.env is
# gitignored; this template is not, so never put a real secret in here.
#
#     cp test/.env.example test/.env
#
# Every name is the same setting as the matching flag, upper-cased with the
# SCHMERZ_ prefix: --push-private-key is SCHMERZ_PUSH_PRIVATE_KEY. Anything
# exported in your shell wins over this file.
#
# Nothing here is needed for an ordinary local run: the launcher starts the
# services with --development, which switches console authentication off.

# --- Console: which collectives the local editor manages -----------------
# With authentication off, everybody is one stand-in identity. By default it
# is in the administrators' group and sees everything. Name other groups here
# to see the console as one collective's editor does — the fixtures use
# buendnis-duesseldorf, buendnis-koeln, buendnis-leipzig, buendnis-sozialstaat.
# SCHMERZ_DEVELOPMENT_GROUPS=buendnis-duesseldorf

# --- Web Push -------------------------------------------------------------
# A VAPID key pair. Without it notifications are written to each reader's
# list and simply not pushed, which is a supported way to run.
# SCHMERZ_PUSH_PUBLIC_KEY=
# SCHMERZ_PUSH_PRIVATE_KEY=
# SCHMERZ_PUSH_SUBJECT=mailto:you@example.org

# --- Reverse geocoding ---------------------------------------------------
# Nominatim needs no key, but its usage policy asks for a contact so an
# operator can be reached before being blocked. Your own address.
# SCHMERZ_GEOCODE_CONTACT=you@example.org

# Set to false to make no request to a geocoder at all. Places an editor names
# are never looked up either way; this only affects pins left unnamed.
# SCHMERZ_GEOCODE_ENABLED=true
